From 53f7358694a4ef7fa70e5cab9176c4c426cedb11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:02:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] gps: wire up A-GNSS, A-GNSS RIL and XTRA assistance

The GNSS module could acquire a fix but had no way to be helped towards one:
SUPL, cell-based reference location and predicted ephemeris all live behind
IGnss extension interfaces the module never asked for, so the nyx methods that
carry them answered NYX_ERROR_NOT_IMPLEMENTED and a device with a SIM got no
benefit from having one.

Fetch IAGnss, IAGnssRil and IGnssXtra after the core interface is up, register a
callback object with each, and map them onto the nyx methods that were
previously unregistered: set_server, data_conn_open/closed/failed,
set_ref_location, set_set_id, update_network_state,
update_network_availability and inject_xtra_data.

The extensions are optional by design - a HAL that does not implement one
answers getExtension* with a null binder rather than an error - so each family
is kept only if both the interface and its setCallback succeeded, and every
method checks that before acting. They are registered unconditionally because
nyx_module_register_method needs the nyx_instance_t that only nyx_module_open
has, while the HAL is not bound until init(); the truthful answer therefore
arrives at call time instead of registration time.

One conversion is not a pass-through, and the compile-time checks are what
caught it: nyx's APN bearer type still follows the legacy GPS HAL numbering
where AGPS_APN_BEARER_IPV4 is 0, whereas HIDL's ApnIpType inserted INVALID at 0
and shifted the rest up. Forwarding the nyx value unchanged would have told the
HAL INVALID for every IPv4 APN, so gps_apn_ip_type_to_hidl() maps it explicitly
and the remaining assistance constants - which do agree - are asserted instead.

Two further asymmetries are handled rather than papered over:
set_ref_location refuses nyx's MAC-address form, which IAGnssRil@1.0 cannot
represent, and requestRefLocCb reports CELLID because that is the only kind
this module can supply.

NI and geofencing remain unimplemented; they need IGnssNi and IGnssGeofencing,
which are still not fetched, and their callbacks are still dropped.

